// PARAM: --analysis parity
// x == 0 && x == 1 is self-contradictory (no integer is both), and so is
// y == 0 && y == 1, so this branch is concretely unreachable. Unlike the
// Sign/Interval/Int siblings of this fixture, the mechanism here is not
// join-arm pollution in bfilter: Parity has no backward_domain
// interpretation at all (Parity_Numeric_Queries.thy -- parity has no
// inv_less/meet instance, so guards cannot refine it), and branch_parity
// (Parity_Transfer.thy) is the identity on every guard, narrowing or not.
// x == 5 therefore comes back UNKNOWN regardless of what the guard says.
// There is no bfilter_lifted for Parity to wire into tf_branch, so unlike
// its siblings this case is not expected to change.
void main() {
  x := __voblint_nondet_int();
  y := __voblint_nondet_int();
  if ((x == 0 && x == 1) || (y == 0 && y == 1)) {
    __voblint_check(x == 5) // UNKNOWN
  } else {
    skip
  }
}
